// Sheet's own "range" field is mapped to "Self" in the source data because
// D&D's real Dream reaches a sleeping creature across any distance (no
// line-of-sight requirement) rather than because the spell targets the
// caster -- the sheet's own `notes` field says so explicitly ("range
// 'special' ... mapped to Self + note"). Mechanically this still needs to
// land on a real target, so `range` here is set to a generous long-range
// value matching this circle's other single-target ranged nightmares
// (phantasmal_killer.ron, mental_prison.ron) rather than literally
// `SelfOnly`, which would make the spell untargetable. Documented here
// rather than silently overriding the sheet's own field without comment.
BasicRanged(
    energy_cost: 90.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    projectile: (
        kind: Simple,
        attack: Some((
            damage: 36,
            damage_kind: Psychic,
        )),
    ),
    projectile_body: Object(BoltFire),
    projectile_speed: 55.0,
    num_projectiles: Value(1),
    meta: (
        school: Some(Illusion),
        source: Some(Arcane),
        // level 5 spell -> min_level 30, the level * 6 convention.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(30)),
    ),
)
